=begin pod

=TITLE App::ModuleAudit

=head1 NAME

App::ModuleAudit - audit locally installed Raku modules

=head1 SYNOPSIS

=begin code :lang<bash>
module-audit scan
module-audit list
module-audit check-upgrades
=end code

=head1 DESCRIPTION

C<App::ModuleAudit> records and inspects the set of Raku modules installed on a
local computer.

The default database location is:

=begin code
~/.module-audit/module-audit.db
=end code

Use C<--db-path> to override the database file.

=head1 COMMON COMMANDS

=item C<module-audit scan>

Scan installed modules and save the current module set.

=item C<module-audit list>

List installed modules and print a summary status line.

=item C<module-audit check-upgrades>

Check installed modules for available upgrades.

=item C<module-audit report>

Print an upgrade report.

=item C<module-audit prune-versions --all>

Preview removal of older installed versions.

=item C<module-audit apply-file --file=modules.txt>

Preview install/update actions from a module list file.

=head1 DETAILED USAGE

See C<docs/USAGE.rakudoc>.

